    "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the measures of the interior angles of a triangle given that they are in the ratio 5:6:7. Let's denote the measures of the angles as \\(5x\\), \\(6x\\), and \\(7x\\), where \\(x\\) is a common multiplier.\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always 180 degrees. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n\\[\n5x + 6x + 7x = 180\n\\]\n\nNext, we combine the terms on the left side of the equation:\n\\[\n18x = 180\n\\]\n\nTo find the value of \\(x\\), we divide both sides of the equation by 18:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{180}{18} = 10\n\\]\n\nNow that we have the value of \\(x\\), we can find the measures of the three angles by substituting \\(x = 10\\) back into the expressions for the angles:\n\\[\n5x = 5 \\times 10 = 50\n\\]\n\\[\n6x = 6 \\times 10 = 60\n\\]\n\\[\n7x = 7 \\times 10 = 70\n\\]\n\nThe smallest interior angle is the one with the smallest measure, which is 50 degrees. Therefore, the measure of the smallest interior angle is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{50}\n\\]",
